## Review freeze

Tested head: `2743a29a2b3b488cce29cebdac7f433fe7227f8f`

(Previously frozen at `0ace785c03cdcc7a34c5aea0d8ea76fb42ea1334`; the head moved by one
commit, "Post-review fixes: resolved timeouts, asserted-by-default provenance", which
lands the two review blockers described below. Full suite re-run green at the new head:
35 passed, 1 skipped — the external G2 gate without its environment variable.)

## Summary

- advances the package/tooling candidate to 0.2.0 while keeping the v0.1 wire contracts stable;
- adds executable readiness gates, clean-wheel dogfood, tamper falsification, compatibility policy, and release documentation;
- validates the Harbor adapter against a private genuine seven-trial archive and records only redacted workspace evidence;
- fixes Harbor null metric and effective wall-time fallbacks found during real-data review;
- resolves effective agent wall-time as min(override base, optional cap) times the resolved multiplier with every component preserved under the Harbor extensions block, so a configured cap can no longer masquerade as an observed effective budget (five regression tests);
- defaults undeclared generic instrument values and plain claims to operator_asserted rather than observed — a pre-adoption evidence-status semantic correction; wire versions unchanged;
- recognizes the observed ATIF v1.5/v1.6 root surface, preserves layered network configuration, avoids inferred completion on unfinished trials, and redacts raw tool/verifier configuration;
- gives Harbor maintainers a focused review path with current unsupported no-ATIF, multi-step, regrade, and job-denominator boundaries;
- documents the product lifecycle: prospective capture setup, post-run sealing, retrospective reprocessing without model compute, and future static comparison reports;
- adds a redacted real comparison showing task-checksum, denominator, and budget drift without making a model-quality claim;
- expands CI across CPython 3.11–3.14 and wheel dogfood on Linux, macOS, and Windows.

## Falsification result

The first branch CI run exposed platform-dependent demo digests on Windows. Demo files now use explicit UTF-8/LF bytes, with a regression test. The follow-up run is green across all jobs:

https://github.com/edward-lcl/eval-evidence/actions/runs/30407125004

## Local verification

- `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v`: 29 tests, green; only external G2 skips without its environment variable.
- Explicit private G2 invocation: passed without a skip on seven genuine Harbor trials.
- Frozen acceptance gate: 31/31 checks passed.
- Clean wheel/sdist build, distribution audit, installed-wheel generic/Harbor dogfood, reference tamper, and bundle tamper: passed.
- Representative discovery measurement: 8,633 genuine Harbor runs in 5.248 seconds, 44,761,088 bytes peak RSS on the recorded machine.

## Honest remaining boundary

G2 remains `unmet` in `docs/READINESS.md`: regular CI does not have an approved sanitized structural fixture or secure fixture access, even though the private local protocol passed. This PR does not create a release tag, publish to PyPI, claim signed attestation, or add live monitoring. Current no-ATIF discovery completeness, multi-step `step_results`, regrade lineage, and job-level denominator/index semantics remain explicitly unsupported pending maintainer review.

## Résultat

Rebase final d ADC-666 directement sur le master qui contient déjà ADC-665 et ADC-648. La branche ne rejoue aucun commit de ses dépendances.

- une transaction native distincte par tentative adaptative ;
- publication seulement après acceptation collective ;
- enveloppes de rejet MPI validées et déterministes ;
- rollback des sorties scientifiques AMR ;
- commit_many simultané Uniform et AMR plat ;
- refus fail-closed des permutations AMR multi-niveaux non conservatives ;
- ProjectAndRecheck publie l identité exacte des projections exécutées ;
- gate M2 sans preuve différée.

## Validation locale post-rebase

- Ruff ciblé : succès ;
- Python ciblé : 29 tests réussis ;
- contrat ProgramContext natif : 13 tests réussis ;
- TUs System, AMR et tests concernés compilés ;
- git diff --check : succès.

Le test AMR history ring a été compilé mais son lien/exécution complète est laissé à la CI pour éviter un second rebuild transitif concurrent.

