## Summary
After creating a project the app navigated to `/project/[id]`, rendered for ~1s, then jumped to `/login`. Cause: the project page's `init()` wrapped **all** setup calls in a single blanket handler that treated any failure as an auth failure:

```ts
try {
  await getMe();
  ...getProjects()...
  await getMessages(id);
  await getFiles(id);
  await startSandbox(id);   // e.g. sandbox/docker fails here
} catch {
  router.push("/login");    // logged the user out even though authenticated
}
```

A freshly created project has no sandbox/files/messages yet, so one of those non-auth calls throws and the generic `catch` redirected an authenticated user to login.

Fix: distinguish real auth (401) errors from everything else.
- `api.ts`: `apiFetch` now throws an `ApiError` carrying `status`; added `isAuthError(err)` helper (`ApiError && status === 401`).
- `project/[id]/page.tsx`: only `getMe()`/`getProjects()` can redirect, and only on `isAuthError`. `getMessages`/`getFiles`/`startSandbox` are each wrapped so a failure is logged but no longer logs the user out.
- `dashboard/page.tsx`: same guard — redirect to `/login` only on `isAuthError`.

`tsc --noEmit` passes; lint output is unchanged from base (pre-existing `no-explicit-any` warnings only).

